{"id": "EUVD-2026-86141", "enisaUuid": "ab9d0a3d-09a8-3939-af5e-37c4173df3da", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\next4: fix circular lock dependency in ext4_ext_migrate\n\nMove iput(tmp_inode) after ext4_writepages_up_write() to avoid a\ncircular lock dependency between s_writepages_rwsem and sb_internal\n(freeze protection).\n\nThe deadlock scenario:\n\n  CPU0 (EXT4_IOC_MIGRATE)        CPU1 (orphan cleanup during mount)\n  ----                           ----\n  ext4_ext_migrate()\n    ext4_writepages_down_write()\n      s_writepages_rwsem (write)\n                                 ext4_evict_inode()\n                                   sb_start_intwrite()   [sb_internal]\n                                   ...\n                                     ext4_writepages()\n                                       s_writepages_rwsem (read) [BLOCKED]\n    iput(tmp_inode)\n      ext4_evict_inode()\n        sb_start_intwrite()         [BLOCKED]\n\nThe tmp_inode is a temporary inode with nlink=0 created solely for\nbuilding the extent tree.  Its eviction does not require\ns_writepages_rwsem protection, so deferring iput() until after\nreleasing the rwsem is safe.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:52:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/452950461241dfed8b1d32e94b227db38c99c5af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ada23457d4748d6e9c36c6f871fc29a6f558c48c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4223231b6860141813637a6413c2371ae4d6fa8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32f7ab52875ec7f800ca67e7176e5743a84baddf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a897682793eba5de51ee6f3152760374afa629cf"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9p82-h2x3-6rrv", "CVE-2026-93269"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2de6764c-5350-3c29-9e72-5d0e54eb1274", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb85f4d23f794e24127f3e562cb3b54b0803f456 <a897682793eba5de51ee6f3152760374afa629cf"}, {"id": "38285b45-fb90-31c7-b894-4cd748275265", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "6c418e85-de61-35dd-af07-095a5a57a70f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb85f4d23f794e24127f3e562cb3b54b0803f456 <452950461241dfed8b1d32e94b227db38c99c5af"}, {"id": "8823c1d4-2d87-35c0-a519-e6dcb0e782d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb85f4d23f794e24127f3e562cb3b54b0803f456 <ada23457d4748d6e9c36c6f871fc29a6f558c48c"}, {"id": "8f248bff-92bc-308d-b1b2-c77a99755e0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb799e163dc2bc1ea0a4820b66f79d32a5e907df"}, {"id": "95c4317b-119a-3955-aca7-827bda76d190", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9.215 <4.10"}, {"id": "96545a11-b72b-3dea-bd40-ba4ebe3b2dfe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "98cdcdbc-65a7-3119-bf8f-2ae2b6404646", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69f8a7991fd93c49096ddd11574db3e7df238b7b"}, {"id": "a3fb5834-c7c5-3e3a-9d77-99b83f4d8a44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a43249c1-5c20-38ed-940e-da9bab30544d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a4b48f6f-7507-326d-97dd-17c414fefbf8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb85f4d23f794e24127f3e562cb3b54b0803f456 <e4223231b6860141813637a6413c2371ae4d6fa8"}, {"id": "acc29ef6-0e9c-314c-bd66-f1a4047ba3cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf20fb73e73a4c4df0328b5297842c5ef34fdd9"}, {"id": "b34e03ee-938d-372f-9041-c4ef7b9a435b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version"